{"toolCallId":"call_25e4530d43d243bb938825530a9edf7e","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"62:| `AI_PROTOCOLS`       | ERROR    | Level 3/3+    | AI execution protocols present                 |\n63-| `LEVEL_MATCH`        | ERROR    | All files     | Level consistent across all spec files         |\n64-| `SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY` | ERROR  | spec docs, goal.md | Anchor sufficiency; for `goal.md` also the durable budget (one limit: fail past 4000) and binding-row existence |\n65-| `FRONTMATTER_VALUES` | WARNING  | packet docs   | `contextType` or `importance_tier` outside sk-create-frontmatter's `frontmatter-values.json`; aliases are legal |\n66-| `SOURCE_TAGS`        | WARNING  | research/ + review/ | `[SOURCE: path:line]` tags that name a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, in packets created after the cutoff |\n67-\n68-> **Partial reference:** The table above covers the most commonly-encountered rules. The authoritative, complete rule set and their canonical severities live in [`runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json`](../../runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json).\n69-\n70-### AC_CLOSURE\n71-\n72-`AC_CLOSURE` decides whether a packet may be closed. It is registered at ERROR severity and runs by default; set `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE=false` to opt out.\n73-\n74-**Rule ID:** `AC_CLOSURE`\n75-\n76-**Scope:** Levels 2, 3 and 3+. Level 1 keeps acceptance criteria inline in `spec.md` and is never gated.\n77-\n78-**Rollout:** forward-only behind `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF` (default `2026-08-30`), compared against the `Created` date in the packet's `spec.md` metadata table. A packet created on or before the cutoff, or whose date cannot be read, is advisory on **every** branch — presence, waiver integrity and completion alike — and is never blocked. A malformed override falls back to the default rather than being compared as a string, which would otherwise grandfather the whole repository. This mirrors the `CANONICAL_SAVE_CUTOFF` pattern rather than introducing a third grandfathering mechanism.\n79-\n80-**Failure modes:**\n81-\n82-| Condition | Result |\n83-|---|---|\n84-| Post-cutoff packet with no `acceptance-criteria.md` | `fail` — the document is required at these levels |\n85-| A row marked `Waived` or `Superseded` naming no ADR | `fail` — an unbacked waiver is not a pass |\n86-| A criterion row that cannot be parsed, or an unbalanced code fence | `fail` — a dropped row would empty the table and close the packet |\n87-| Duplicate criterion ids | `fail` — the tally is ambiguous |\n88-| A row citing an ADR that `decision-record.md` does not contain | `fail` — the record is the whole justification |\n89-| A packet claiming completion with an `Unmet` row | `fail` — this is the closure gate |\n90-| An `Unmet` row while the packet is still in progress | `info` — work in progress is expected to carry open criteria |\n91-| Pre-cutoff packet | `info` — grandfathered |\n92-\n--\n632:## 10. AI_PROTOCOLS\n633-\n634-**Severity:** ERROR\n635-**Description:** Validates that Level 3 and 3+ specs include AI execution protocol sections for agent guidance. For Level 3+, missing protocol components are reported as errors.\n636-\n637-### Required for Level 3+\n638-\n639-| Component             | Location        | Purpose                           |\n640-| --------------------- | --------------- | --------------------------------- |\n641-| AI Execution section  | plan/tasks.md   | Main protocol header              |\n642-| Pre-Task Checklist    | plan/tasks.md   | Steps before starting any task    |\n643-| Execution Rules       | plan/tasks.md   | TASK-SEQ, TASK-SCOPE constraints  |\n644-| Status Format         | plan/tasks.md   | How to report progress            |\n645-| Blocked Protocol      | plan/tasks.md   | What to do when stuck             |\n646-\n647-### Scoring\n648-\n649-- Level 3: Should have protocol section (warning if missing)\n650-- Level 3+: Must have at least 3/4 components (error if fewer)\n651-- Phase parent: skipped. Under the lean trio policy its `plan.md` and `tasks.md` live in the child folders, which carry the protocol.\n652-\n653-### Detection Patterns\n654-\n655-```markdown\n656-## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL         ← Main section\n657-### Pre-Task Checklist           ← Component 1\n658-### Execution Rules              ← Component 2\n659-### Status Reporting Format      ← Component 3\n660-### Blocked Task Protocol        ← Component 4\n661-```\n662-\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"7ef5c3","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
