{"toolCallId":"call_63da30b6483b4be6a9b8a5f1abb7a3a1","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"FILE_EXISTS | error |  | Validates required spec documents for the declared documentation level.\nPLACEHOLDER_FILLED | error |  | Rejects unfilled template placeholders in authored spec documents.\nCOMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER | error |  | Rejects ephemeral finding markers inside HTML comments in authored spec documents.\nSCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED | error |  | Rejects scaffold-signature markers in required docs when spec.md claims Complete status.\nSTATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY | error |  | Advisory-by-default check that spec.md and implementation-summary.md status fields classify to the same delivery state.\nLEVEL_DECLARED | info |  | Reports whether the documentation level was declared or inferred.\nAC_COVERAGE | info |  | Default-on advisory (non-blocking) scan for acceptance-criteria traceability coverage; set SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=false to opt out.\nAC_CLOSURE | error |  | Gates packet closure on acceptance-criteria.md at Levels 2, 3 and 3+; unmet criteria block a completion claim and a waiver must cite an ADR that exists. Packets created before the cutoff stay advisory.\nANCHORS_VALID | error |  | Checks anchors in each spec doc whose template defines them, ignoring fenced code; a phase parent is exempt, and research/research.md and review/review-report.md are skipped as free-form workflow documents. Errors: a doc with no anchors, an anchor opened twice, never closed, closed but never opened, or closed more times than it is opened. Nesting is also an error: an anchor opened inside another, closed before it is opened, or closed while another is still open, though markers quoted in inline code are ignored by the nesting check; an adr-NNN anchor may hold adr-NNN-* anchors. Template order is not checked.\nFRONTMATTER_MEMORY_BLOCK | error |  | Validates canonical _memory continuity frontmatter blocks.\nMERGE_LEGALITY | error |  | Validates generated merge payloads against target anchor shape.\nSPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY | error |  | Checks implementation-summary sufficiency after save/write flows.\nCROSS_ANCHOR_CONTAMINATION | error |  | Detects route/category mismatches before generated content is merged.\nPOST_SAVE_FINGERPRINT | error |  | Verifies post-save fingerprints for generated writes.\nTOC_POLICY | error |  | Enforces table-of-contents placement policy.\nAI_PROTOCOLS | error |  | Validates AI execution protocol sections in high-governance specs.\nCOMPLEXITY_MATCH | error |  | Checks declared level against content complexity signals.\nFOLDER_NAMING | error |  | Validates numbered spec-folder naming conventions.\nFRONTMATTER_VALID | error |  | Validates YAML frontmatter structure and required semantic values.\nFRONTMATTER_VALUES | warn |  | Warns when a packet document's contextType or importance_tier is outside the shared list in sk-doc/sk-create-frontmatter/assets/frontmatter-values.json. Aliases are legal.\nSOURCE_TAGS | warn |  | Warns when a path:line citation inside a [SOURCE: ...] tag in a packet's research or review artifacts names a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, using sk-doc's citation resolver. Packets created on or before the cutoff are skipped. A pass means the path and line exist, not that they support the claim.\nGREP_CONVENTION | error |  | Checks every markdown document in a spec folder against the greppable-corpus convention: frontmatter variant, trigger phrase quality, anchor grammar and naming.\nLEVEL_MATCH | error |  | Checks required files match the declared documentation level.\nGRAPH_METADATA_PRESENT | warn |  | Checks generated description and graph metadata are present.\nGRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT | warn |  | Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids missing on-disk phase children the writer would add (advisory unless SPECKIT_CHILD_DRIFT_ENFORCE=true).\nGRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_IDENTITY | error |  | Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids entries whose leading path identity is not the packet's own current identity (stale rename residue the refresh writer now prunes).\nGRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE | warn |  | Validates graph-metadata.json shape: required packet/derived blocks, last_active_child_id pointer integrity for phase parents.\nMETADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY | error |  | Advisory-by-default check that description.json, graph-metadata.json, and continuity ids match the real on-disk spec-folder path.\nDESCRIPTION_SHAPE | warn |  | Validates description.json shape: required name/description/level keys present and well-typed.\nNORMALIZER_LINT | error |  | Strict-only lint for duplicated runtime normalizer helpers.\nSPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY | error |  | Verifies inline markdown references resolve within spec docs.\nTEMPLATE_SOURCE | error |  | Checks SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE provenance markers.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED | error |  | Ensures canonical saves include a root spec reference.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED | error |  | Ensures canonical saves include source document references.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED | error |  | Ensures canonical save lineage metadata is present.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_PACKET_IDENTITY_NORMALIZED | error |  | Checks canonical save packet identity normalization.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_DESCRIPTION_GRAPH_FRESHNESS | error |  | Checks generated description/graph freshness for canonical saves.\nCONTINUITY_FRESHNESS | error | strict | Strict-mode freshness check for continuity frontmatter. The rule reports warn by default and escalates to fail under SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS_ENFORCE; the ceiling here has to allow that escalation, since a warn ceiling would silently cap it.\nGENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY | error | strict | Validates description.json and graph-metadata.json through the shared schemas plus path-prefix and status-enum invariants, error under strict behind a grandfather report mode.\nGENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT | error | strict | Re-derives a folder and reports drift between the stored description/causal_summary and the current docs, read-only, error under strict only when the drift-gate flag is on and otherwise grandfather report mode.\nLINKS_VALID | warn |  | Scans the system-spec-kit skill's own markdown for wikilinks whose target file does not exist. The target is always this skill, never the validated packet.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"1ceeef","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_6d29e6dff26e47e4a8fdd9f57c2bde01","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"    .filter((docName) => !FREEFORM_WORKFLOW_DOCS.has(docName))\n    .filter((docName) => fs.existsSync(templatePathForName(templateNameForDoc(level, docName))));\n}\n\nfunction anchors(content: string): string[] {\n  return [...stripFences(content).matchAll(/<!--\\s*ANCHOR:([A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_-]*)\\s*-->/gu)].map((match) => match[1]);\n}\n\nfunction validateFileExists(folder: string, level: SpecKitLevel): ValidationEntry {\n  const requiredDocs = level === 'phase' ? docsForLevel(level) : requiredDocsForLevel(folder, level);\n  const missing = requiredDocs.filter((docName) => !fs.existsSync(path.join(folder, docName)));\n  if (level === 'phase') {\n    for (const required of ['description.json', 'graph-metadata.json']) {\n      if (!fs.existsSync(path.join(folder, required))) missing.push(required);\n    }\n  }\n  return missing.length === 0\n    ? entry('FILE_EXISTS', 'pass', `All required files present for Level ${level}`)\n    : entry('FILE_EXISTS', 'error', `Missing ${missing.length} required file(s) for Level ${level}`, missing);\n}\n\n// Canonical spec-doc placeholder markers. Mirrors check-placeholders.sh\n// (YOUR_VALUE_HERE + NEEDS_CLARIFICATION underscore/space). Mustache `{{...}}`\n// is intentionally NOT included: it is not the canonical spec-doc placeholder\n// syntax and legit spec-doc content uses it, so flagging it false-positives.\nconst PLACEHOLDER_MARKER_RE = /<YOUR_VALUE_HERE:|\\[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:|\\[NEEDS_CLARIFICATION:|\\[NEEDS CLARIFICATION:/u;\n\nfunction validatePlaceholders(folder: string, level: SpecKitLevel): ValidationEntry {\n  const findings: string[] = [];\n  // A workflow loop owns the freeform docs and rewrites them whole at\n  // synthesis, so a scaffolded skeleton's markers are not an author's debt.\n  for (const docName of validationDocsForLevel(folder, level).filter((docName) => !FREEFORM_WORKFLOW_DOCS.has(docName))) {\n    const content = readIfExists(path.join(folder, docName));\n    if (!content) continue;\n    const lines = content.split(/\\r?\\n/u);\n    // Track fenced code blocks: a line starting with ``` toggles in_code and is\n    // itself skipped, matching check-placeholders.sh awk behavior.\n    let inCode = false;\n    lines.forEach((line, index) => {\n      if (/^\\s*```/u.test(line)) {\n        inCode = !inCode;\n        return;\n      }\n      if (inCode) return;\n      const match = PLACEHOLDER_MARKER_RE.exec(line);\n      if (!match) return;\n      // Skip inline-backtick-wrapped markers: if the matched marker is\n      // immediately preceded by a backtick on this line, it is escaped content\n      // (parity with the shell rule's grep -v of backtick-wrapped cases).\n      if (match.index > 0 && line.charAt(match.index - 1) === '`') return;\n      findings.push(`${docName}:${index + 1}: ${line.trim().slice(0, 120)}`);\n    });\n  }\n  return findings.length === 0\n    ? entry('PLACEHOLDER_FILLED', 'pass', 'No unfilled template placeholders found')\n    : entry('PLACEHOLDER_FILLED', 'error', `${findings.length} placeholder(s) found`, findings);\n}\n\nfunction validateTemplateSource(folder: string, level: SpecKitLevel): ValidationEntry {\n  const missing = authoredDocsForLevel(level, folder).filter((docName) => {\n    const content = readIfExists(path.join(folder, docName));\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"6abd24","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
